{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 20, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark to thee O traveler bold who dost embark\nUpon a voyage to fair Nippon’s shore\nWhere cherry blossoms bloom and ancient temples mark\nThe sacred paths of time now evermore.\nLet this itinerary thee guide with grace and might\nThrough lands of wonder and traditions bright.\n\n**Upon the First Morn in Tokyo’s Lively Light**\nAwake thou in Nihonbashi where modern meets old\nTo Senso-ji’s grand gates do thou now betake\nWhere lanterns glow and incense whispers low\nIn Asakusa’s heart where pilgrims partake\nIn fortune’s cast upon wooden planks so plain\nThen feast on ramen rich with broth so deep\nAt Ichiran where steaming cups remain\nA solace sweet for weary souls to keep.\n\n**To the Samurai’s Rest Where History Lies**\nForward to the castle of Edo’s might\nWhere shoguns ruled with wisdom stern and wise\nClimb the steps of fortress walls so high\nAnd gaze upon the land where emperors rise\nAt Ueno’s park do tarry not too long\nFor cherry blossoms dance in spring’s soft song.\n\n**Upon the Trains Swift as the Phoenix’s Flight**\nTo Kyoto now with haste do thou repair\nWhere geisha glide like shadows in the night\nAnd temples stand in harmony with air\nAt Kinkaku-ji’s gold where sunlight gleams\nAnd Fushimi’s shrines with torii gates so tall\nDo bow thy head and pray with wishes deemed.\n\n**Through Bamboo’s Whisper Where the Spirit Calls**\nTo Arashiyama’s grove of stalks so tall\nWhere time itself doth seem to still and fall\nThen venture forth to Gion’s lantern-lit streets\nWhere teahouses hum with tales of yore\nA cup of matcha sip with gentle beats\nOf shamisen’s strings that sing evermore.\n\n**To Nara’s Deer Where Ancient Mysteries Lie**\nA day’s journey to sacred deer that roam\nAt Todai-ji’s heart where Buddha smiles\nUpon thee with eyes of timeless home\nFeed them with crackers from thy hand so kind\nAnd mark the moment where the past aligns.\n\n**Back to Tokyo’s Pulse Where Neon Burns**\nWith temples filled and stomachs pleasantly full\nReturn to Shibuya’s crossing where the world\nDoth pause and gawk at lights that never dull\nThen dine on sushi fresh as ocean’s breath\nAt Tsukiji’s market where the morning’s catch\nIs served with skill and grace beyond compare’s death.\n\n**To Mount Fuji’s Shadow Where the Sky Begins**\nIf time and luck do favor thy quest\nAscend the slopes where pilgrims tread in chains\nOf old and gaze upon the mountain’s crest\nThat pierces heavens with its fiery pains.\nOr rendezvous with hot springs where steam ascends\nIn Hakone’s baths where weary flesh depends.\n\n**A Farewell Feast Where Tokyo’s Splendor Ends**\nOn thy last eve in Ginza’s gleaming glow\nIndulge in wagyu beef so rich and rare\nWith saké poured in cups of porcelain’s flow\nAnd lanterns raised to mark the end of care.\n\n**As Dawn Doth Break on Thy Final Day**\nTo Narita’s gates with memories untold\nDo thou depart yet keep within thy heart\nThe tales of Japan both fierce and bold\nWhere every street a sonnet doth impart\nAnd every soul a verse of joy hath charted\nIn fair Nippon’s land so wondrous and arted.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.16029712557792664}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.003225721186026931}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -2.9867587089538574}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0396350733935833}, {"token": "e", "logprob": -0.0018114125123247504}, {"token": " O", "logprob": -1.9671317338943481}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -1.5850106477737427}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.005440903827548027}, {"token": " bold", "logprob": -0.2810775637626648}, {"token": " who", "logprob": -1.1738370656967163}, {"token": " dost", "logprob": -0.19078697264194489}, {"token": " embark", "logprob": -0.9746053218841553}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.8960992097854614}, {"token": "Upon", "logprob": -0.3245784342288971}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.6471376419067383}, {"token": " voyage", "l